(6194098, 914278, 81362, '<td valign="top">Very pretty, could do well in free study. Not an obvious fit for from the knees down challenge.</td>', 'Very pretty, could do well in free study. Not an obvious fit for from the knees down challenge.', '2010-10-17 20:32:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6194129, 914087, 30982, '<td valign="top">The making of this shot:  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=913978" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30982/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_913978.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30982/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_913978.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30982/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_913978.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>In a private thread (and this is for the benefit of any who may read the comments after the challenge) a teammate was remarking at how easily shots like this seem to come for Ben, yet how very few can accomplish this sort of thing with the energy and complexity that he achieves.  Since I was fortunate enough to be there when this shot was taken, I can pass along some state secrets... (and then head into the witness protection program!)  He does take care to consider what he''s after - he thinks that through.  In this instance, he was using a neutral density filter since as you can see from the "how it happened" shot, we still had quite a bit of strong light.  But after he takes into consideration what he''s after and how best to technically achieve that goal, he lets things happen.  He just lets the picture come to him, so to speak.  No elaborate light setup, no reflectors, no posing of models.  Just a late Sunday afternoon at the beach, a couple of amazing young ladies, and a guy with a camera who is in tune with the world around him.</td>', 'The making of this shot:    In a private thread (and this is for the benefit of any who may read the comments after the challenge) a teammate was remarking at how easily shots like this seem to come for Ben, yet how very few can accomplish this sort of thing with the energy and complexity that he achieves.  Since I was fortunate enough to be there when this shot was taken, I can pass along some state secrets... (and then head into the witness protection program!)  He does take care to consider what he''s after - he thinks that through.  In this instance, he was using a neutral density filter since as you can see from the "how it happened" shot, we still had quite a bit of strong light.  But after he takes into consideration what he''s after and how best to technically achieve that goal, he lets things happen.  He just lets the picture come to him, so to speak.  No elaborate light setup, no reflectors, no posing of models.  Just a late Sunday afternoon at the beach, a couple of amazing young ladies, and a guy with a camera who is in tune with the world around him.', '2010-10-17 21:31:07.000000', NULL, 1),
